code: background job tooling with completion notices

Long-running shell commands used to hold the agent loop hostage:
lofi.bash returned only after the command finished, so a five-minute
build blocked five minutes of chat. Add a jobs subsystem that spawns
commands into detached processes, exposes lofi.job_spawn/status/read/
wait/kill bindings, logs stdout+stderr to per-job files under the
session tmp dir, and lets the agent tick, wait on, or reap any of
them through a /job modal.

Completion surfaces through a new transient prompt kind. The job
runner emits a Notice TurnStart with the exit summary; the agent
loop records the turn under PromptKind::Notice so it is stamped
separately from real user prompts, replays with the same kind after
a restart, and renders in the UI with a hollow-bullet subtle marker
plus muted italic body to read as system output rather than chat.
Kind state rides along on TurnStart for the live session and via a
TurnPrompt recorder event for resume, so a mid-session compaction or
reload does not lose the distinction.

Companion UI work: a /job list+drill-in modal showing runtime, exit
status, and a paged log view; tighter modal frames with primary-color
edges and one-cell padding so stacked pickers do not dock to the
edges of the screen.